        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8c2b89b4-556d-5024-be7e-75122e0517a8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, Roger Taylor, Taylor Hawkins, Lisa Carver\n- Music groups: Sugarland, Soul Miner's Daughter, Jennifer Nettles Band, Foo Fighters, Queen\n- Songs: “Everyday America”, “Heaven for Everyone”\n- Places: Atlanta\n- Events: Planet Rock poll\n\nFacts:\n- Before Sugarland was formed, Jennifer Nettles fronted the Atlanta-based bands Soul Miner's Daughter and Jennifer Nettles Band.\n- Jennifer Nettles is best known as the lead singer of the duo Sugarland alongside Kristian Bush.\n- In 2005, Roger Taylor was voted the eighth-greatest drummer in classic rock history by radio listeners in a Planet Rock poll.\n- Roger Taylor was acclaimed by Foo Fighters drummer Taylor Hawkins as one of the most influential rock drummers of the 1970s and 1980s.\n- “Everyday America” was written by Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, and Lisa Carver.\n- “Heaven for Everyone” was written by Roger Taylor.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
